WEBVTT

00:00:00.646 --> 00:00:03.970
Fair test: same starting
conditions, one intended

00:00:03.970 --> 00:00:05.872
difference, and repeat measurements

00:00:06.657 --> 00:00:10.292
Third, a respirometer
investigates oxygen uptake.

00:00:10.647 --> 00:00:15.453
In a sealed apparatus, an absorbent
removes the carbon dioxide produced.

00:00:15.642 --> 00:00:19.687
As oxygen is used, gas volume
or pressure changes, moving a

00:00:19.696 --> 00:00:21.627
colored marker in a narrow tube

00:00:22.327 --> 00:00:24.658
Why remove the carbon dioxide?

00:00:25.385 --> 00:00:28.901
Otherwise, the gas being produced
could offset oxygen being removed.

00:00:29.384 --> 00:00:31.937
Temperature must be controlled
too, because warming a

00:00:31.939 --> 00:00:33.469
gas can change its volume.

00:00:34.055 --> 00:00:37.836
Use a comparison setup and your teacher's
safety procedure for the absorbent

00:00:38.658 --> 00:00:42.929
So a moving marker isn't automatically
a respiration speedometer unless

00:00:42.929 --> 00:00:44.414
we control the other causes

00:00:44.833 --> 00:00:49.987
Final challenge: I ask, you answer, and
anyone watching can answer before you.

00:00:50.563 --> 00:00:51.748
What is respiration?

00:00:52.502 --> 00:00:54.637
A chemical process in living cells

00:00:54.638 --> 00:00:57.957
that releases energy
from glucose Beautiful.

00:00:58.585 --> 00:01:01.872
Where does most energy release
in aerobic respiration occur

00:01:01.888 --> 00:01:03.439
in animal and plant cells?

00:01:04.258 --> 00:01:08.366
Mitochondria, not the nucleus,
and not only in the lungs

00:01:09.115 --> 00:01:11.302
Write the aerobic word equation

00:01:12.046 --> 00:01:15.671
Glucose plus oxygen gives
carbon dioxide plus water.

00:01:16.177 --> 00:01:18.670
Energy is released, not created.

00:01:18.928 --> 00:01:23.205
Your tissues may stand down
Why are folds useful inside

00:01:23.209 --> 00:01:23.273
a

00:01:23.276 --> 00:01:24.135
mitochondrion?

00:01:25.025 --> 00:01:29.520
They provide a large surface area
for some of the reactions Yeast

00:01:29.522 --> 00:01:31.534
without oxygen produces what?

00:01:32.269 --> 00:01:34.833
Ethanol and carbon dioxide.

00:01:35.254 --> 00:01:40.819
The carbon dioxide helps dough rise
And human anaerobic respiration?

00:01:41.677 --> 00:01:46.234
Lactic acid, much less energy per
glucose than aerobic respiration.

00:01:46.629 --> 00:01:50.339
I won't copy the yeast equation
When do plants respire?

00:01:51.248 --> 00:01:52.327
Day and night.

00:01:52.795 --> 00:01:56.432
Photosynthesis needs light,
but respiration carries on

00:01:56.975 --> 00:01:58.753
What turns limewater milky?

00:01:59.536 --> 00:02:03.210
Carbon dioxide, and a fair
experiment needs controls,

00:02:03.349 --> 00:02:04.932
not just an exciting balloon

00:02:05.735 --> 00:02:06.614
That's the method.

00:02:06.874 --> 00:02:11.211
Explain the process, use precise
words, and connect each structure

00:02:11.216 --> 00:02:12.935
or observation to its reason.

00:02:13.317 --> 00:02:17.039
Exact marks depend on the question
and mark scheme, but clear

00:02:17.039 --> 00:02:18.742
science is your best protection

00:02:19.489 --> 00:02:23.023
Glucose unlocked, energy
released, teacher rescued.

00:02:23.486 --> 00:02:26.560
Now I can take the stairs without
calling my lungs a chemical factory
